{
  "cells": [
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# Sequence-to-Sequence Models Notebook\n\n> Hands-on Build It and Exercises."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Build It"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 1: an encoder"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "import torch"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "import torch.nn as nn"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        ""
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "class Encoder(nn.Module):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def __init__(self, src_vocab_size, embed_dim, hidden_dim):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        super().__init__()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.embed = nn.Embedding(src_vocab_size, embed_dim, padding_idx=0)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.gru = nn.GRU(embed_dim, hidden_dim, batch_first=True)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def forward(self, src):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        e = self.embed(src)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        outputs, hidden = self.gru(e)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        return outputs, hidden"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "`outputs` has shape `[batch, seq_len, hidden_dim]` \u2014 one hidden state per input position. `hidden` has shape `[1, batch, hidden_dim]` \u2014 the final step. Lesson 08 said \"pool over outputs for classification.\" Here we keep the last hidden state as the context vector, and ignore the per-step outputs."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 2: a decoder"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "class Decoder(nn.Module):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def __init__(self, tgt_vocab_size, embed_dim, hidden_dim):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        super().__init__()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.embed = nn.Embedding(tgt_vocab_size, embed_dim, padding_idx=0)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.gru = nn.GRU(embed_dim, hidden_dim, batch_first=True)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.fc = nn.Linear(hidden_dim, tgt_vocab_size)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def forward(self, token, hidden):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        e = self.embed(token)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        out, hidden = self.gru(e, hidden)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        logits = self.fc(out)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        return logits, hidden"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Decoder is called one step at a time. Input: a batch of single tokens and the current hidden state. Output: vocabulary logits for the next token and the updated hidden state."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 3: training loop with teacher forcing"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def train_batch(encoder, decoder, src, tgt, bos_id, optimizer, teacher_forcing_ratio=0.9):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    optimizer.zero_grad()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    _, hidden = encoder(src)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    batch_size, tgt_len = tgt.shape"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    input_token = torch.full((batch_size, 1), bos_id, dtype=torch.long)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    loss = 0.0"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    loss_fn = nn.CrossEntropyLoss(ignore_index=0)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    for t in range(tgt_len):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        logits, hidden = decoder(input_token, hidden)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        step_loss = loss_fn(logits.squeeze(1), tgt[:, t])"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        loss += step_loss"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        use_teacher = torch.rand(1).item() < teacher_forcing_ratio"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        if use_teacher:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            input_token = tgt[:, t].unsqueeze(1)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        else:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            input_token = logits.argmax(dim=-1)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    loss.backward()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    optimizer.step()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return loss.item() / tgt_len"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Two knobs worth naming. `ignore_index=0` skips loss on padding tokens. `teacher_forcing_ratio` is the probability of using the true token vs. the model's prediction at each step. Start at 1.0 (full teacher forcing) and anneal down to ~0.5 over training to close the exposure-bias gap."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 4: inference loop (greedy)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "@torch.no_grad()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def greedy_decode(encoder, decoder, src, bos_id, eos_id, max_len=50):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    _, hidden = encoder(src)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    batch_size = src.shape[0]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    input_token = torch.full((batch_size, 1), bos_id, dtype=torch.long)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    output_ids = []"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    for _ in range(max_len):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        logits, hidden = decoder(input_token, hidden)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        next_token = logits.argmax(dim=-1)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        output_ids.append(next_token)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        input_token = next_token"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        if (next_token == eos_id).all():"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            break"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return torch.cat(output_ids, dim=1)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Greedy decoding picks the highest-probability token at every step. It can wander off: once you commit to a token, you cannot unsay it. **Beam search** keeps the top-`k` partial sequences alive and picks the highest-scoring complete one at the end. Beam width 3-5 is standard."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 5: the bottleneck, demonstrated"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Train the model on a toy copy task: source `[a, b, c, d, e]`, target `[a, b, c, d, e]`. Increase sequence length. Observe accuracy."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "seq_len=5   copy accuracy: 98%"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "seq_len=10  copy accuracy: 91%"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "seq_len=20  copy accuracy: 62%"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "seq_len=40  copy accuracy: 23%"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "A single GRU hidden state cannot losslessly memorize a 40-token input. The information is there at every encoder step, but the decoder only sees the last state. Attention fixes this directly."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Exercises"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "1. **Easy.** Implement the toy copy task. Train a GRU seq2seq on input-output pairs where the target equals the source. Measure accuracy at lengths 5, 10, 20. Reproduce the bottleneck.\n2. **Medium.** Add beam search decoding with beam width 3. Measure BLEU on a small parallel corpus against greedy. Document where beam search wins (usually last tokens) and where it makes no difference.\n3. **Hard.** Fine-tune `facebook/bart-base` on a 10k-pair paraphrase dataset. Compare the fine-tuned model's beam-4 output to the base model's on held-out inputs. Report BLEU and pick 10 qualitative examples."
      ]
    }
